segments.text:
On the thirteenth day of the month of May, in the year one thousand nine hundred and ninety-six, at the Sergeant's School of Arms (EsSA), the witness, 1st Lieutenant of the Marine Infantry MARCIO LUIZ PASSOS TIBERIO, IDT 043753693-1 Min.Ex, son of MAURO CARVALHO TIBERIO and ILMA PASSOS TIBERIO, residing at 4 Rua Sagrada Familia #67, Bairro Santa Tereza, in this city, was questioned about the event recorded in Portaria n°033-Aj-G2, of May 10, 1996, to which he was read and declared the following:

That on January 22, Monday, he arrived at the Sergeant's School of Arms at 07:00 hours, the quarter where he works, holding the position of Chief of the 3rd Section of the BCSv and Commander of the Police Platoon of the Army (Pel PE), to command the morning formation of the BCSv, after which he performed tasks in the 3rd Section of the BCSv until approximately 11:17... -x.s:xjue immediately after he went for lunch at the officers' casino, returning at 13:00 for the afternoon formation with the Pel PE;

That from then until 16:00 hours, he was engaged in tasks in the 3rd Section of the BCSv;

That from this moment onwards, he performed a military physical training until approximately 17:15 hours;

That immediately after, he went to his home, where he was found. wife, Sr’ CLEIDE ALVES DE OLIVEIRA Tiki; who, around 7:30 PM, went, together with his wife, to visit the home of Sr ENIO CUPOLILLO, resident at 4 Paraguay Street #266, Jardim América neighborhood, returning to his home around 10:00 PM; who, on January 23, 1996, Tuesday, attended EsSA for the morning graduation, and also performed work at the 3rd Sector of BCSv, teaching at the School; who, at 1:15 PM, also participated in the afternoon graduation with BCSy, performing work in the same sector until 4:00 PM; who, at 5:30 PM, went to his home, where his wife was waiting for him; who, around 8:30 PM, went, together with his wife, to the residence of Sr ILDOVAN AUGUSTO, resident on Avenue... Chico Lima, number 139, Bairro Vila Lima, returning home around 10:00 PM. When asked if there is anyone who can attest to his work routine, he responded that there is, the 1st Lieutenant Cav LUIS HENRIQUE AMORIM, Commander of the CCSv. When asked if he had knowledge of walks from EsSA to VARGINHA-MG undergoing maintenance, he responded that he did not, as this issue is not within his scope, and he had heard nothing about it. When asked if he knows or has had contact with Mr. UBIRA2:*.2.A RODRIGUES and VICTORIO PACACCINI, he responded that he does not, as he does not know them. As nothing more was said or asked, this deposition is concluded, and it has been read and found to be...: properly signed by this investigating officer and the witness.
